---
/* Our Approach diagram. Inlined rather than loaded as an image so each part
   can be moved on its own; the flat Figma export is regrouped here into base /
   ring / core / node / orbit layers, with every path copied verbatim so the
   at-rest render is identical to /assets/decor/approach-diagram.svg.

   One thing is deliberately not copied: the backdrop-filter foreignObject
   layer Figma exports under each frosted disc. A browser ignores that layer in
   an image tag, so it adds nothing to the diagram as it ships today, but once
   inlined it runs — and blurs the platform ring into near-invisibility. The
   discs' translucent white fill, which is what actually reads as frosted, is
   untouched.

   The three words are live <text>, not the outlined glyphs Figma exported —
   they are the one part of the drawing the positioning can change, so they are
   set in the site's own heading font (.ad-word in home.css) and re-typed rather
   than re-drawn. The record mark beside "Record" is a lucide file glyph placed
   on the centre the old gear used.

   Motion lives in home.css under "Approach diagram — motion". Nothing is
   hidden without JS: the armed (hidden) state is only applied once the script
   has confirmed it can also un-hide it. */

