  <!-- Motes. The field of light the disc is dusted with.

       Two turbulence layers, each thresholded down to a sparse scatter of
       seeds, then blurred and re-amplified so a seed arrives as a soft
       bloom instead of a lit pixel. The blur is what makes the glow; the
       amplification is what keeps it from disappearing into the blur.

       This replaces a single layer at baseFrequency 5 whose features were
       finer than one device pixel and whose alpha was thresholded hard to
       0 or 1 — so every mote was an aliased pinprick with no falloff.
       Against white that read as grain. Against black it read as static.

       The two frequencies do different work: the fine layer carries the
       texture, the coarse one scatters a handful of wider, dimmer blooms
       through it so the field has some depth instead of one uniform size.
       flood-color and flood-opacity are CSS properties, so the hue and the
       overall intensity are set from home.css with the rest of the
       diagram's palette. -->
